  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mrs.Renuka Devi vs State Rep.By on 18 July, 2023 Author: N.Anand Venkatesh",
    "facts": "2.The issue involved in this case is covered by the earlier judgments of the Apex Court and this Court and hence, the main petition itself is taken up for hearing. 3.The respondent has filed a private complaint against four accused persons u/s 59(1) and 51 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (hereinafter referred as 'the Act'). The petitioner has been arrayed as A.3 in the complaint. The main allegation as found in the complaint is that the food that was prepared in the hotel was inspected and it was sent for analysis and it was found that it is substandard and unsafe. In view of the same, this criminal original petition has been lodged by the respondent.",
    "arguments": "5.The petitioner has been arrayed as A-3 on the ground that she is the Director of the A-1 Company. Section 66 of the Act provides for offences by Companies. Section 66(1) of the Act states that every person who at the time the offence was committed was in charge of and was responsible to the Company for the conduct of the Company, shall be deemed to be guilty of the offence. 6.Section 66(2) of the Act provides that where the offence as was committed with the consent or connivance of or is attributable to any neglect on the part of any director, then such a Director can be proceeded against and punished.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5.The petitioner has been arrayed as A-3 on the ground that she is the Director of the A-1 Company.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Section 66 of the Act provides for offences by Companies. Section 66(1) of the Act states that every person who at the time the offence was committed was in charge of and was responsible to the Company for the conduct of the Company, shall be deemed to be guilty of the offence. 6.Section 66(2) of the Act provides that where the offence as was committed with the consent or connivance of or is attributable to any neglect on the part of any director, then such a Director can be proceeded against and punished."
  },
